    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="0464" n="452" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg452"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.77/731a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-06T20:00:00-04:00">August 6, 1943—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>396. Department’s instruction 242, July 3.<anchor n="19" xml:id="d481-f1"/>
                    Soviet note dated July 27 states that Russian Ambassador Tehran will be
                    instructed to inform Iranian Government that Soviet Government has no objections
                    to participation of American troops in control over southern part of
                    Trans-Iranian railroad. Text of note follows by air mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d481-f1" n="19" xml:id="d481-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it transmitted texts of the Soviet note of May 11, <ref
                        target="#pg448">p 448</ref>, and the Department’s note in reply, June 15,
                        <ref target="#pg466">p. 466</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
